@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Partner and Customer Ticket Integration
	Testing ticket changes when a project has partners and customers on it.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View partner removal attempt with open ticket when customers are remaining
	Last partners with open tickets should not be removed when customers are remaining.

	Given I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I attempt to remove a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker from the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner" who still has an open Zendesk ticket
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken"

Scenario: View customer removal attempt with open ticket when partner is remaining
	Last customers with open tickets should not be removed when partners are remaining.

	Given I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	When I remove a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I attempt to remove a user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA" who still has an open Zendesk ticket
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken"

Scenario: View developer removal attempt with open ticket when partner and watcher is remaining
	Last developers with open tickets should not be removed when partners and watchers are remaining.

	Given I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I attempt to remove a user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer from the project with the code "ZENOSBA" who still has an open Zendesk ticket
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

